 ### [Continuous Level Transitions](5275-continuous-level-transitions.md)
-Maintains continuity of the 3D scalar field at boundaries where adjacent bricks are rendered at different levels of detail (LOD). It adapts the textures of finer-level bricks to interpolate correctly from the coarser level, restricting transitions to a difference of at most one level.
+Continuous Level Transitions is a technique that maintains continuity of the 3D scalar field at boundaries where adjacent bricks are rendered at different levels of detail (LOD). It sets itself apart from fixed-boundary bricking by adapting finer-level brick textures to interpolate correctly from coarser levels, restricting transitions to a difference of at most one level. It should be chosen when multi-resolution rendering is required to balance quality and performance across varying distances or regions of interest [G].
 
